# Contributing to ResPdfSharp

Thanks for your interest in contributing!

## License of contributions

ResPdfSharp is MIT licensed (see LICENSE and NOTICE).

By submitting a pull request or commit to this repository you confirm that:

1. You wrote the change yourself or otherwise hold the right to contribute it, and it does
   not bring AGPL-licensed code from upstream PDFsharp 6.5.0 or later (see FORK.md,
   "Import policy").
2. You grant the ResPdfSharp project and its downstream users a perpetual, worldwide,
   royalty-free, irrevocable MIT license to your contribution as contributed here.
3. You are allowed to make this grant (your employer/contract, if any, does not forbid it).

This is a license grant, not a copyright assignment: you keep the copyright of your change.
A commit message sign-off (`Signed-off-by: Name <email>`, DCO-style) is appreciated but the
submission itself counts as the grant above.

## Upstream changes

Changes from upstream PDFsharp after the fork baseline (`fork-start`, commit 8d818d5) are
AGPL/commercial and generally cannot be cherry-picked; they must be re-implemented
independently or carry documented MIT-compatible permission. Explain in the pull request
where an idea (not code) was taken from.

## Branding

Do not reintroduce upstream logos or branding. "PDFsharp" may be mentioned only to describe
the origin of the code, never as the name of this product.
